  "backtest_data_needs": "M1",
  "python_conversion_notes": "Straightforward conversion. All indicators have direct Python equivalents (ta-lib or pandas_ta). Key considerations: (1) SL/TP are in points not pips — need to clarify pip/point semantics in Python. (2) Session filter uses broker server hour — must use UTC+offset logic. (3) No new-bar guard means signals are checked every tick but effectively fire once because of the position_check gate. (4) CTrade.Buy/Sell with SL/TP maps to market orders with stop/take. (5) Stochastic crossover detection requires comparing previous bar K vs D values — implement as shift(1) comparison in pandas. (6) The RSI buy zone (10-25) and sell zone (80-90) are unusual — RSI must be extremely oversold/overbought as confirmation within an established trend, meaning pullback entry in strong trends.",
